From: Gnomsa <gnomsa88@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda/cs8409: disable generic automute on Apple path

The Apple CS8409/CS42L83 path performs jack routing through its own
unsolicited-event handling.  Prevent the generic parser from exposing an
Auto-Mute Mode control and do not register generic automute callbacks.

WirePlumber restores ALSA mixer controls when a desktop session starts.  If
Auto-Mute Mode is present, that restore can enter call_update_outputs() through
the Apple driver's automute callback and leave the HDA control path wedged.

Authored-by: Gnomsa <gnomsa88@gmail.com>
Copyright (c) 2026 Gnomsa
---
 patch_cirrus_apple.h | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/patch_cirrus_apple.h b/patch_cirrus_apple.h
index 9a9311e..10b5b94 100644
--- a/patch_cirrus_apple.h
+++ b/patch_cirrus_apple.h
@@ -1752,6 +1752,14 @@ static int cs_8409_apple_parse_auto_config(struct hda_codec *codec)
 
         myprintk("snd_hda_intel: cs_8409_apple_parse_auto_config\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * The Apple CS8409 path handles jack routing itself.  Do not let the
+	 * generic HDA parser create an "Auto-Mute Mode" control: userspace
+	 * restores that control during login and call_update_outputs() then
+	 * enters callbacks which are not part of this routing implementation.
+	 */
+	spec->gen.suppress_auto_mute = 1;
+
 	err = snd_hda_parse_pin_defcfg(codec, &spec->gen.autocfg, NULL, 0);
 	if (err < 0)
 		return err;
@@ -2946,7 +2954,10 @@ static int patch_cs8409_apple(struct hda_codec *codec)
 
 	spec->gen.pcm_capture_hook = cs_8409_capture_pcm_hook;
 
-	spec->gen.automute_hook = cs_8409_automute;
+	/* Jack routing is handled by the CS42L83 unsolicited-event path above. */
+	spec->gen.automute_hook = NULL;
+	spec->gen.hp_automute_hook = NULL;
+	spec->gen.line_automute_hook = NULL;
 
 
 	// so this seems to be how we setup volume controls for the headphones
-- 
